  "summary": "Before leaving my recent employer, the Department of Corrections, I worked in customer service/hospitality for five years. Over the years, I've gained skills in communication, attention to detail, patience, and creative problem-solving. With these skills, I decided to make a leap of faith and pursue a career in Software Engineering by attending Flatiron School. \n\nAfter becoming a Full-Stack Engineer, my goal is to develop websites or apps for clients and companies. I would love to work close to clients while creating projects that fit their needs and demands for business or more!\n\nI'm always seeking more significant challenges and opportunities to better myself, and I've always had a knack for creating or developing projects that allowed me to flex my creativity. As a kid, I would make skits and comedic posts online to make people laugh and brighten up their days. These hobbies taught me to use editing software such as Adobe Premiere Pro, Lightroom, and Media Encoder. I would love to apply these skills as well in my new career in software engineering.",
